msgid "Hello, World"
msgstr ""

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md:8
msgid ""
"Let us jump into the simplest possible Rust program, a classic Hello World "
"program:"
msgstr ""

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md:12
msgid "// Copyright 2024 Google LLC\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md:13
msgid "// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md:16
msgid "\"Hello 🌍!\""
msgstr ""

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md:20
msgid "What you see:"
msgstr ""

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md:22
msgid "Functions are introduced with `fn`."
msgstr ""

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md:23
msgid "The `main` function is the entry point of the program."
msgstr ""

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md:24
msgid "Blocks are delimited by curly braces like in C and C++."
msgstr ""

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md:25
msgid "Statements end with `;`."
msgstr ""

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md:26
msgid "`println` is a macro, indicated by the `!` in the invocation."
msgstr ""

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md:27
msgid "Rust strings are UTF-8 encoded and can contain any Unicode character."
msgstr ""

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md:32
msgid ""
"This slide tries to make the students comfortable with Rust code. They will "
"see a ton of it over the next four days so we start small with something "
"familiar."
msgstr ""

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md:35
msgid "Key points:"
msgstr "重點："

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md:37
msgid ""
"Rust is very much like other languages in the C/C++/Java tradition. It is "
"imperative and it doesn't try to reinvent things unless absolutely necessary."
msgstr ""

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md:40
msgid "Rust is modern with full support for Unicode."
msgstr ""

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md:42
msgid ""
"Rust uses macros for situations where you want to have a variable number of "
"arguments (no function [overloading](../control-flow-basics/functions.md))."
msgstr ""

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md:45
msgid ""
"`println!` is a macro because it needs to handle an arbitrary number of "
"arguments based on the format string, which can't be done with a regular "
"function. Otherwise it can be treated like a regular function."
msgstr ""

#: src/types-and-values/hello-world.md:49
msgid ""
"Rust is multi-paradigm. For example, it has powerful [object-oriented "
"programming features](https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch17-00-oop.html), and, "
"while it is not a functional language, it includes a range of [functional "
"concepts](https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch13-00-functional-features.html)."
msgstr ""
